Subject: [PATCH] clocksource: add SoCLabs MicroBlaze-V AXI timer clockevent (v3, productized)

S-mode kernel tick on the Xilinx AXI Timer via the AXI INTC external
interrupt (SEIP), for AMD MicroBlaze-V silicon whose Sstc stimecmp never
raises a deliverable STIP and whose mip.STIP is stuck once set (both
board-proven 2026-07-16 on MPS3 KU115). rdtime stays the clocksource;
only the clockevent moves. Binds only "soclabs,mbv-timer" - inert on
every other device tree.

Lineage:
 v1  first plan-D driver: tick delivered ("first tick via SEIP" at
     0.021 s) but the tick engine died ~33 s into boot - the level-typed
     INTC input re-latches ISR between handle_level_irq's early ack and
     the posted T0INT-clear landing, and the spurious-re-entry dance
     loses on silicon timing.
 v2  plan-C-v2-proven ack sequence in the ISR (T0INT W1C + read-back,
     then own-bit IAR scrub + read-back): silicon-proven stable, 2500+
     ticks, zero spurious.
 v3  (this version) productized, no functional change to the proven v2
     register sequence: DT binding document added (errata record, the
     rationale for dropping "sstc" from the deployed DT, and the
     re-enable path once AMD ships fixed IP); real Kconfig help; error
     paths complete (irq disposal, INTC unmap, zero-frequency guard,
     NULL event_handler guard); bring-up breadcrumbs demoted to
     pr_debug tripwires - the console is quiet by default; printk
     prefix is now "soclabs-mbv-timer:" (was "pland:" in bring-up
     images - update console greps accordingly).

diff -Naur a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/timer/soclabs,mbv-timer.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/timer/soclabs,mbv-timer.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/timer/soclabs,mbv-timer.yaml	1970-01-01 01:00:00.000000000 +0100
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/timer/soclabs,mbv-timer.yaml	2026-07-17 10:32:55.894834804 +0100
@@ -0,0 +1,128 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 OR BSD-2-Clause
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/timer/soclabs,mbv-timer.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: SoCLabs linux_soc (AMD MicroBlaze-V) AXI Timer S-mode tick
+
+maintainers:
+  - SoC Labs <noreply@soclabs.org>
+
+description: |
+  Errata binding for the SoCLabs "linux_soc" platform (AMD MicroBlaze-V
+  RV32IMAC hart, Arm MPS3 / XCKU115 carrier). The node is an ordinary
+  Xilinx LogiCORE AXI Timer (see timer/xlnx,xps-timer.yaml); prepending
+  "soclabs,mbv-timer" to its compatible list opts the node in to the
+  timer-soclabs-mbv clockevent driver, which delivers the kernel tick
+  from timer channel 0 as a plain S-mode external interrupt through the
+  AXI INTC. Without the prepended compatible the node reverts to a plain
+  AXI Timer (PWM/counter uses) and the driver is inert.
+
+  Why this binding exists - the silicon errata (board evidence
+  2026-07-16, three debug windows on MPS3 KU115):
+
+    E1  Sstc dead: writing stimecmp never produces a deliverable S-mode
+        timer interrupt, although the time counter (rdtime, Zicntr) runs
+        correctly at 100 MHz. The CSR write is accepted; the interrupt
+        never arrives.
+
+    E2  mip.STIP stuck-once-set: injecting STIP from M-mode (the retired
+        OpenSBI "plan C" workaround, which took the AXI timer on MEIP and
+        set mip.STIP by hand) delivers exactly one interrupt, after which
+        no M-mode write can clear STIP again ("mip.STIP will not clear"
+        tripwire), livelocking the kernel in its timer handler.
+
+    (A third, independent erratum - wfi never wakes - is handled by a
+    separate kernel idle-path workaround, not by this binding.)
+
+  External interrupt delivery is healthy on the same silicon: MEIP and
+  SEIP are both taken, mideleg=0x222 delegates supervisor interrupts, and
+  the AXI INTC dispatches through irq-riscv-intc/irq-xilinx-intc. Hence
+  the tick, and only the tick, is moved onto the external-interrupt path;
+  rdtime remains the clocksource.
+
+  Why "sstc" is DROPPED from riscv,isa-extensions in the deployed DT
+  -------------------------------------------------------------------
+  The deployed device tree deliberately removes "sstc" from the cpu
+  node's riscv,isa-extensions (it is generated that way by the platform's
+  mk_dtb_pland.sh). Three reasons, all load-bearing:
+
+    1. Advertising sstc makes the kernel program stimecmp (dead per E1)
+       and register the riscv-timer clockevent; nothing may ever depend
+       on STIP given E2.
+    2. It removes any reliance on clockevent rating arbitration: this
+       driver is the ONLY tick provider, so a tick-less stall is
+       unambiguous evidence of a SEIP-delivery failure, not of a device
+       selection accident.
+    3. On models/silicon where the time CSR is not wired for the sstc
+       comparator flow, a stimecmp access can trap (observed as an
+       illegal-instruction panic in riscv_clock_event_stop on the QEMU
+       amd-microblaze-v-generic negative control). Never advertising the
+       extension makes that access impossible.
+
+  Re-enable path once AMD ships fixed MicroBlaze-V IP
+  ---------------------------------------------------
+  When a corrected core (stimecmp raises a deliverable STIP, mip.STIP
+  clearable, ideally C_INTERRUPT_WAKEUP=1 so wfi wakes) is proven - use
+  the platform's bare-metal fw_mspin discriminator first, then a kernel
+  boot watching for the riscv-timer tick - revert in this order:
+
+    1. restore "sstc" in the cpu node's riscv,isa-extensions;
+    2. drop the "soclabs,mbv-timer" prefix from this node's compatible
+       (the node reverts to a plain AXI Timer; this driver goes inert);
+    3. optionally disable CONFIG_SOCLABS_MBV_TIMER;
+    4. the separate wfi-idle workaround is reverted independently, only
+       after wfi wakeup is proven on the fixed core.
+
+  Steps 1-2 are pure device-tree changes: one kernel binary supports
+  both the errata silicon and fixed silicon.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    items:
+      - const: soclabs,mbv-timer
+      - const: xlnx,xps-timer-1.00.a
+
+  reg:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  interrupts:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description:
+      AXI INTC input fed by the timer's interrupt output. The input is
+      level-typed (C_KIND_OF_INTR=0); the driver's ISR ack sequence
+      depends on level (not edge) semantics.
+
+  clock-frequency:
+    description:
+      Timer s_axi_aclk rate in Hz (100000000 on linux_soc). Used to
+      program tick deltas; must match the synthesized clock exactly or
+      timekeeping drifts.
+
+  clocks:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  clock-names:
+    const: s_axi_aclk
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+  - interrupts
+  - clock-frequency
+
+# The node stays a valid xlnx,xps-timer node (xlnx,count-width etc.)
+additionalProperties: true
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    timer@41c00000 {
+        compatible = "soclabs,mbv-timer", "xlnx,xps-timer-1.00.a";
+        reg = <0x41c00000 0x10000>;
+        interrupt-parent = <&axi_intc>;
+        interrupts = <0 4>;
+        clock-frequency = <100000000>;
+        xlnx,count-width = <32>;
+        xlnx,one-timer-only = <0>;
+    };
diff -Naur a/drivers/clocksource/Kconfig b/drivers/clocksource/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/clocksource/Kconfig	2026-07-17 10:31:23.838885977 +0100
+++ b/drivers/clocksource/Kconfig	2026-07-17 10:33:13.020313551 +0100
@@ -782,4 +782,28 @@
           Enables the support for NXP System Timer Module found in the
           s32g NXP platform series.
 
+
+config SOCLABS_MBV_TIMER
+	bool "SoCLabs MicroBlaze-V AXI timer clockevent"
+	depends on RISCV || COMPILE_TEST
+	select TIMER_OF
+	help
+	  Clockevent driver that delivers the S-mode kernel tick from a
+	  Xilinx LogiCORE AXI Timer through the AXI INTC as a normal
+	  external interrupt (SEIP).
+
+	  This is a silicon-errata workaround for the SoCLabs linux_soc
+	  platform (AMD MicroBlaze-V on Arm MPS3): on that silicon the
+	  Sstc stimecmp comparator never raises a deliverable S-mode
+	  timer interrupt and mip.STIP is stuck once set, so neither the
+	  architected timer nor an SBI-injected STIP can provide the
+	  tick. The rdtime clocksource is unaffected and is not touched.
+
+	  The driver binds only the "soclabs,mbv-timer" compatible and
+	  is inert on every other device tree. See
+	  Documentation/devicetree/bindings/timer/soclabs,mbv-timer.yaml
+	  for the errata record, why "sstc" is dropped from the deployed
+	  device tree, and the re-enable path back to the architected
+	  timer once fixed IP is available.
+
 endmenu
